Root cause:
The bug was caused by the struct `mlx4_uverbs_ex_query_device_resp` being defined in a driver-specific header file (`mlx4_ib.h`), which made it inaccessible to user-space applications that needed to interact with the user API for mlx4. This struct is essential for the user API, and its placement in a driver header file violated the principle of exposing necessary structures in the user API headers. The patch corrects this by moving the struct definition to the appropriate user API header file (`mlx4-abi.h`), ensuring that it is properly exposed for user-space access.
